# op-agent-engine environment
#
# ./agent-init.sh writes this file (mode 0600): it creates the OpenProject
# users and stores their tokens and the model provider key here. It does not
# ask for GitHub credentials; add GH_TOKEN (and the optional reviewer values
# below) before starting the stack. This example is only the reference for the
# variables and their defaults. Compose reads the real file automatically; it
# is never mounted. Never commit the real file: it contains API tokens.

# --- OpenProject (required) -------------------------------------------------

OP_BASE_URL=https://openproject.example.com
# Project identifier(s): one identifier, a comma-separated list, or * for
# every active project that has the GIT_REPO project attribute set.
OP_PROJECT=my-project
# API token of the engine user; make that user an administrator.
OP_ENGINE_TOKEN=replace-with-agent-engine-api-token

# --- The repository work packages are implemented in ------------------------
#
# Each project is read from the PROJECT attribute named GIT_REPO. Create it
# once in OpenProject (Administration -> Projects -> Project attributes), use
# the text format, and make it available for all projects. Values are GitHub
# repositories: owner/name or a github.com URL.

# Clone directory under WORKSPACE_ROOT for a single explicit project.
# Otherwise the directory is derived from GIT_REPO (and made unique).
# GITHUB_REPO_DIR=repository
# Optional override; by default the engine asks git for the remote default
# branch when it prepares the workspace.
# GITHUB_DEFAULT_BRANCH=main

# --- Agent models and tokens (required) ------------------------------------

# Model for every agent: <provider>/<model>. The provider is the prefix, and
# it also selects the credential variable below (see docs/CONFIG.md). Leave this
# unset when every agent names its own model below.
# AGENT_MODEL=openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash-1017
# Optional: one agent can use another model from the SAME provider.
# AGENT_MODEL_FRONTEND=openrouter/deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-chat
# AGENT_MODEL_BACKEND=
# AGENT_MODEL_DESIGNER=
# AGENT_MODEL_VFX=
# AGENT_MODEL_AUDIO=
# AGENT_MODEL_REVIEWER=

OP_TOKEN_FRONTEND=replace-with-frontend-api-token
OP_TOKEN_BACKEND=replace-with-backend-api-token
OP_TOKEN_DESIGNER=replace-with-designer-api-token
OP_TOKEN_VFX=replace-with-vfx-api-token
OP_TOKEN_AUDIO=replace-with-audio-api-token
OP_TOKEN_REVIEWER=replace-with-reviewer-api-token

# GitHub token used to clone, push and look up pull requests. The account must
# be able to write to every repository named by a project's GIT_REPO attribute.
GH_TOKEN=replace-with-github-token

# Optional: a second GitHub account for codeReviewer. Protected repositories can
# require the approving/merging account to differ from the PR author; set this
# token to an account with pull-request write access to enable the reviewer to
# approve and merge as that account. The reviewer's git commit identity also
# switches to the values below (defaults: codeReviewer / the OpenProject email
# domain). Leave both token lines unset to keep one shared GitHub identity.
# GH_TOKEN_REVIEWER=
# GIT_REVIEWER_NAME=codeReviewer
# GIT_REVIEWER_EMAIL=codeReviewer@agent-engine.local

# --- Model provider (required: one key for your AGENT_MODEL) ----------------
# pi reads its provider key from the environment; there is no auth.json or
# settings.json to mount. ./agent-init.sh asks for the key of the provider in
# AGENT_MODEL and writes it here, so normally you do not edit this.
# The full provider/variable table is in docs/CONFIG.md.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Local llama.cpp server (pi's built-in llama.cpp provider). Use a model such as
# AGENT_MODEL=llama.cpp/qwen2.5-coder-7b. The engine writes the per-run Pi model
# configuration. The URL must be reachable from inside the engine container;
# LLAMA_API_KEY is optional unless llama-server was started with --api-key.
# LLAMA_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.10:8080
# LLAMA_API_KEY=

# --- Provisioning (only ./agent-init.sh and `provision`) -------------------

# An administrator token used to create users and memberships. The script asks
# for it on each run and does not store it.
# OP_PROVISION_TOKEN=

# --- OpenProject object names (defaults match a stock instance) ------------

# OP_AGENT_FIELD=AGENT
# OP_ENGINE_USER=agent-engine
# OP_AGENT_ROLE=Agent Worker
# OP_EMAIL_DOMAIN=agent-engine.local
# OP_STATUS_NEW=New
# OP_STATUS_IN_PROGRESS=In Progress
# OP_STATUS_READY_FOR_REVIEW=Ready for Review
# OP_STATUS_IN_TESTING=In Testing
# OP_STATUS_ON_HOLD=On Hold
# OP_STATUS_REJECTED=Rejected
# OP_STATUS_CLOSED=Closed

# --- Limits and timing ------------------------------------------------------

POLL_INTERVAL_SECONDS=60
MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS=1
# Concurrent runs per agent (default 1). The global limit above still applies.
# Every run gets its own worktree; this only controls how many may run at once.
MAX_RUNS_PER_AGENT=1
MAX_REJECTIONS=3
MAX_CRASH_RETRIES=2
RUN_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600
AGENT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=3600
STOP_GRACE_SECONDS=60
# Run directories and stale worktrees older than this are removed by
# `docker compose run --rm cleanup` (nothing schedules it; add a cron entry on
# the host, see the README).
RUN_RETENTION_DAYS=30
ENGINE_PAUSED=false
LOG_LEVEL=INFO

# --- Dashboard --------------------------------------------------------------
# Read-only web UI, served by the `dashboard` compose service and published on
# 127.0.0.1 only. Change the bind address only behind a reverse proxy: the
# dashboard has no authentication. DASHBOARD_HOST (the bind address inside the
# container) is set to 0.0.0.0 by the image.
DASHBOARD_BIND=127.0.0.1
DASHBOARD_PORT=8765

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Git identity for the commits the agents make. Defaults to OP_ENGINE_USER and
# OP_ENGINE_USER@OP_EMAIL_DOMAIN.
# GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=agent-engine
# GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=agent-engine@agent-engine.local

# Read by compose, not by the engine:
# OP_AGENT_ENGINE_TAG=latest
